  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The length of an elastic string is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;when the tension is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>, and '<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;when the tension is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>. The length in metre when the tension is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>, is</p>\r"
  },
